Triśiras rebukes Rāvaṇa grief as unworthy of lord of worlds --- Triśiras cites Rāvaṇa Brahmā spear armor bow chariot promises Rāma fall --- Rāvaṇa embraces sons sends them with Mahōdara Mahāpārśva guards --- Six warriors mount elephant chariot horse march with roaring host --- Monkeys demons clash with trees rocks swords amid dust blood --- Narāntaka pierces seven hundred monkeys revels in flesh strewn path --- Sugrīva commissions Aṅgada to slay horseman --- Aṅgada endures spear slaps horse dead endures fist on head --- Aṅgada crushes chest of Narāntaka with mountainlike fist --- Gods monkeys roar as foremost foe falls Aṅgada exults